4. Knowledge corpus and evaluation material
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

backend/corpus/ holds a small development corpus: short paraphrases, in Serbian, of published sources, each with a
citation, and the author's own development notes. The corpus is licensed per document, separately from the MIT
licence of the code: backend/corpus/manifest.yaml gives each document's source, URL and terms, and those terms,
not LICENSE, govern the passages of that document. As of this version:

  - fao56 (FAO Irrigation and Drainage Paper 56) and fao_iwm (FAO irrigation water management): short paraphrases
    with citation. The source texts remain under FAO copyright and the FAO terms of use
    (https://www.fao.org/contact-us/terms/); they are cited, not redistributed, and the MIT licence grants no
    rights in them.
  - s2_docs (Copernicus Data Space Ecosystem product documentation): short paraphrases with citation, under the
    terms of that documentation.
  - dev_notes (the author's development notes; not an expert source): MIT, as stated in the manifest.

A document whose terms do not allow redistribution is to be published as metadata only (title, URL, terms); a locally
rebuilt corpus can be checked against the corpus hash stored with every run. The development scenarios in
backend/eval/scenarios/dev/ are the author's own work and are covered by LICENSE.

The development corpus is not the corpus of any reported experiment; see docs/limitations.md.

